3f5c6eec209dd638d2ac880e29fc35fab7f8d6c30bde8c09216fc785ecdc4ec3" "q-76597/selection/962565a04febce5dcbcdfcf10c038379cdfbe6c4ad5ea36f6a2e26d4f9b0c838"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76597" :question/id #uuid "5d332029-2d80-5568-84eb-f48d67119b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-76597" :question/problem "If $\\,u(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,v(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$, find $Aw(t)$ where $w(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u(t)$ and $v(t)$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ the superposition principle guarantees that \n\n$$\ncu(t)+dv(t)\n$$\n\n is also a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for all $c,d\\in R.$\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\nw(t)=9u(t)+2v(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $w$ is a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ So, in order to find $Aw(t)$ we just need to find ${w}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Aw & ={w}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(9{e}^{t})^{′} \\\\ (2{e}^{2t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76597/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318f129c-066d-50bd-934a-90722ba4fc93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection/28fd3cdcd04d985a74c6097c5327fd79d8c24160923caad6e315048ec4eddd8a" :answer/id #uuid "b7a72b9c-bbfb-5337-b520-ea5570b93eb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection/a6258c49080d7379382beda20d14c6f40e6d557f228d0b37a91125a86129ec00" :answer/id #uuid "300de9b3-97fc-565f-9142-4a669f49452f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}30{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 12{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection/c425312407cc1e4c214a3c6a42a8d853756f77bba4d0892fc16d269d6636c0b7" :answer/id #uuid "ae7e903d-9a6e-5074-8a59-829dc3cc8ebe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}30{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 12{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection/942c649afddec6ae933414138828949061b7256a5b0a1ef5b6c5dc52810442ce" :answer/id #uuid "fbd7e5f3-924d-53a2-ac9e-26cb95806431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection/d81f585df9d982ad49b10337897587238ced858d30e9fb1c03954e93b1f52111" :answer/id #uuid "3bc80ff6-981a-56f7-a462-23ab984d4f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Aw=[\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -6{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61065926-0885-5c4e-b91e-e29217dab21b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76602/selection/28fd3cdcd04d985a74c6097c5327fd79d8c24160923caad6e315048ec4eddd8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-76602/selection/28fd3cdcd04d985a74c6097c5327fd79d8c24160923caad6e315048ec4eddd8a" "q-76602/selection/a6258c49080d7379382beda20d14c6f40e6d557f228d0b37a91125a86129ec00" "q-76602/selection/c425312407cc1e4c214a3c6a42a8d853756f77bba4d0892fc16d269d6636c0b7" "q-76602/selection/942c649afddec6ae933414138828949061b7256a5b0a1ef5b6c5dc52810442ce" "q-76602/selection/d81f585df9d982ad49b10337897587238ced858d30e9fb1c03954e93b1f52111"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76602" :question/id #uuid "4f6678b6-2c25-5e0a-b02d-0f73823bf62a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76602" :question/problem "If $\\,u(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,v(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$, find $Aw(t)$ where $w(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -6{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u(t)$ and $v(t)$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ the superposition principle guarantees that \n\n$$\ncu(t)+dv(t)\n$$\n\n is also a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for all $c,d\\in R.$\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\nw(t)=-4u(t)-6v(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $w$ is a solution to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ So, in order to find $Aw(t)$ we just need to find ${w}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Aw & ={w}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-4{e}^{-5t})^{′} \\\\ (-6{e}^{-3t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 18{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318f129c-066d-50bd-934a-90722ba4fc93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1fb4222b-bef5-510b-81f7-7a59ef630c18" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d28f3fef-088f-5d50-9074-8914cf3ae9aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "21960f41-79d3-5875-a45b-9f4d4cac9086" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "bdac7e87-c803-54ed-8765-f1a508589ef0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7b6a6ae6-6ef6-5e3f-a845-5893f7226672" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6672b5b-947e-53ca-b7bb-3d3e6ea137a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-330297/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-330297/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-330297/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-330297/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-330297/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-330297/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330297" :question/id #uuid "a4494cb8-4770-534e-9ebf-f865a2fdba57" :question/math-academy-id "q-330297" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+1\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $3$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330297/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "fde49f9f-48be-512d-998f-f9a0c01a96b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a102ce85-8b9e-5e47-a61b-72f7df5b9c9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bbd50b60-cbaf-533a-b322-f31679f2d1eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "79e6203e-d6ff-5841-8792-13a27ced0ad2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f42b1c70-de7c-56da-8033-e07cb54841ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd3189c-81a1-54b8-a38d-c7b78185ce5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-330302/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer-field/choices ["q-330302/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-330302/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-330302/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-330302/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-330302/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330302" :question/id #uuid "ad686aec-973d-5f95-9289-1f54c1e48676" :question/math-academy-id "q-330302" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)={x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "83a8a3d0-7014-5fc9-9a3f-c57cb66bff6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ff3e1548-961f-58cc-91da-f89e1d1661ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0c0dee42-1c99-5d8d-b851-d147047f0b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "789777b4-9f87-5a47-a72e-fceb61905319" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c416c1d0-34f1-5f99-8a4a-2276986e9c2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f985b96-21e2-5ec1-af64-3823f90be05f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-330309/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer-field/choices ["q-330309/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-330309/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-330309/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-330309/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-330309/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330309" :question/id #uuid "d3d983f3-b2d9-52a7-973a-a729856357d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-330309" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-7\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- ${x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-7\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-7\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)={x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
